<article class="env-lemma" id="035R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/035R">Lemma <span data-tag="035R">29.55.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral, Japanese scheme. The normalization $\nu : X^\nu \to X$ is a finite morphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the definition (Properties, Definition <a href="/tag/033S" data-tag="033S">28.13.1</a>) and Lemma <a href="/tag/035P" data-tag="035P">29.55.3</a>. Namely, in this case the lemma says that $\nu ^{-1}(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A))$ is the spectrum of the integral closure of $A$ in its field of fractions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>